.TH UTIME 3 "May 9, 1985"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
utime \- set file times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <sys/types.h>
.sp
utime(\fIchar *file\fP, \fItime_t timep[2]\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.ft B
This interface is obsoleted by and implemented using utimes(2).
.ft R
.PP
The
.B utime
call
uses the
`accessed' and `updated' times in that order
from the
.I timep
vector
to set the corresponding recorded times for
.IR file .
.PP
The caller must be the owner of the file or the super-user.
The `inode-changed' time of the file is set to the current time.
.SH SEE ALSO
utimes(2), stat(2)
